58: for \(i=0,2\). For \(i=1\) the last two coordinates are
59: \((v,u)\). In each case \(\zeta uv=zn_0n_1=q\).
60: The second new chart uses
61: \((\zeta',u',v')=(n_1/n_0,zn_0,n_0)\), with the same
62: constant interchange for \(i=1\). It has
63: \(\zeta'=\zeta^{-1},(u',v')=\zeta(u,v)\).
64: These formulas are the two quotient charts of the rank-one matrix
65: \[
66:  \begin{pmatrix}n_0&n_1\\zn_0&zn_1\end{pmatrix}.       \tag{CF.6}
67: \]
68: They identify the common complement and both native normal bundles
69: by the actual Cox construction. For the normal interchange at
70: \(i=1\), use the explicit path
71: \[
72:  S_t=\frac12
73:  \begin{pmatrix}
74:  1+e^{\pi it}&1-e^{\pi it}\\
75:  1-e^{\pi it}&1+e^{\pi it}
76:  \end{pmatrix},\qquad 0\le t\le1.                    \tag{CF.6a}
77: \]
78: Its eigenspaces are the two constant lines spanned by
79: \((1,1)\) and \((1,-1)\), with eigenvalues \(1,e^{\pi it}\).
80: Thus \(S_t^*S_t=1\), \(S_0=1\), and
81: \(S_1=(\begin{smallmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{smallmatrix})\).
82: It commutes with the transition \(z\,1\) and therefore acts on
83: the whole native normal bundle. It is independent of the source
84: loop parameter. Its oriented real lift conjugates the two
85: Spin factors through constant conjugations, which preserve
86: both integral third degrees.
87: 
88: Here are the full unit maps. Write the old two periods as GF.2,
89: with unit matrix \(A=(A_{rs})\). The new generators are the
90: columns of \(Q_i\) in that period basis. The actual new units are
91: \[
92:  A'_{rs}=\prod_{h,j}A_{hj}^{(Q_i^{-1})_{rh}(Q_i)_{js}}. \tag{CF.7}
93: \]
94: In the three cases their matrices are
95: \[
96:  A'_0=\begin{pmatrix}
97:  A_{11}A_{21}&A_{12}A_{22}/(A_{11}A_{21})\\
98:  A_{21}&A_{22}/A_{21}
99:  \end{pmatrix},
100: \]
101: \[
102:  A'_1=\begin{pmatrix}
103:  A_{11}/A_{12}&A_{12}\\
104:  A_{11}A_{21}/(A_{12}A_{22})&A_{12}A_{22}
105:  \end{pmatrix},
106: \]
107: \[
108:  A'_2=\begin{pmatrix}
